Error: Jet.MarkedFunctionValue: `bump` can't be used as a function value because its parameter `x` is `^`
  --> Tests/UI/marked_function_value.jet:17:26
    |
 17 |     hooks: Hooks{on_int: bump, on_text: consume}
    |                          ^^^^
 Why: A function type gives each parameter plain read access unless it marks a write (`fn(^T)`) or a take (`fn(^^T)`), so a value of `bump` would drop the `^` its parameter declares
 Fix: Call `bump` directly, mark the parameter in the function type (`fn(^T)`), or pass a lambda that makes that call
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.MarkedFunctionValue

